From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TheDBP <TheDBP@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 04:34:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] binder: stop clang rejecting the deliberate binder_alloc type
 mismatch

clang makes -Wincompatible-pointer-types fatal, so six errors in
binder_alloc.c end the build:

  binder_alloc.c:222: assigning to 'struct binder_lru_page **' from
  'struct binder_lru_page *'
  binder_alloc.c:232: passing 'struct binder_lru_page **' to parameter of
  type 'struct page **'

The mismatch is intentional downstream. 83b0b662b5e8 partially reverted
binder to get the IR blaster working, leaving binder_update_page_range()
with the pre-LRU body that treats alloc->pages as "struct page **" while
binder_alloc.h kept struct binder_lru_page; 63626be73f11 then quieted the
resulting warnings by changing the local's declaration instead of the body.
GCC accepted that and it is what 22.2 ships.

So suppress rather than correct: rewriting the function to upstream LRU
form would restore the path that revert deliberately removed, and IR is why
it was removed. CFLAGS_binder_alloc.o keeps the diagnostic everywhere else.
---
 drivers/android/Makefile | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/android/Makefile b/drivers/android/Makefile
index a01254c43ee3..ae542ff001c9 100644
--- a/drivers/android/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/android/Makefile
@@ -1,4 +1,15 @@
 ccflags-y += -I$(src)			# needed for trace events
 
 obj-$(CONFIG_ANDROID_BINDER_IPC)	+= binder.o binder_alloc.o
+
+# binder_alloc.c carries a deliberate type mismatch, not an accident: 83b0b662b5e8 partially
+# reverted binder to get the IR blaster working, which left binder_update_page_range() treating
+# alloc->pages as the pre-LRU "struct page **" while binder_alloc.h kept struct binder_lru_page,
+# and 63626be73f11 ("Fix a myriad of warnings") settled the mismatch in the declaration rather
+# than the body. GCC warned and shipped; clang makes -Wincompatible-pointer-types fatal.
+#
+# Suppressed for this one object rather than fixed, because writing the function back to upstream
+# LRU form would re-enable exactly the code path that revert removed, and the IR blaster is the
+# thing it was removed for. Scoped to the file so no other driver loses the diagnostic.
+CFLAGS_binder_alloc.o += -Wno-incompatible-pointer-types
 obj-$(CONFIG_ANDROID_BINDER_IPC_SELFTEST) += binder_alloc_selftest.o
